From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 02:53:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix, "getattr" with a default swallowed other exceptions and
 left them set

With a default, the "BUILTIN_GETATTR" helper returned it for any error
of the attribute lookup, while only clearing "AttributeError". Code went
on with the default instead of raising, and the next call noticed the
still set exception and raised "SystemError" about it. Only an
"AttributeError" gives the default now, as with CPython.

Fixes #4061

Co-authored-by: wtfyd-agent[bot] <328989958+wtfyd-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
---
 nuitka/build/static_src/HelpersBuiltin.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/nuitka/build/static_src/HelpersBuiltin.c b/nuitka/build/static_src/HelpersBuiltin.c
index 3e798b41a..f5c36715b 100644
--- a/nuitka/build/static_src/HelpersBuiltin.c
+++ b/nuitka/build/static_src/HelpersBuiltin.c
@@ -738,10 +738,14 @@ PyObject *BUILTIN_GETATTR(PyThreadState *tstate, PyObject *object, PyObject *att
 
     if (result == NULL) {
         if (default_value != NULL) {
+            // Only an "AttributeError" means the default, anything else is
+            // raised, as "getattr" does.
             if (HAS_ERROR_OCCURRED(tstate)) {
-                if (EXCEPTION_MATCH_BOOL_SINGLE(tstate, GET_ERROR_OCCURRED(tstate), PyExc_AttributeError)) {
-                    CLEAR_ERROR_OCCURRED(tstate);
+                if (!EXCEPTION_MATCH_BOOL_SINGLE(tstate, GET_ERROR_OCCURRED(tstate), PyExc_AttributeError)) {
+                    return NULL;
                 }
+
+                CLEAR_ERROR_OCCURRED(tstate);
             }
 
             Py_INCREF(default_value);
